  "body": "This accomplishes a number of goals:\n- Fix #1485 by removing \"set up the request\" and \"process the\n  response\" in favor of the more encompassing \"perform the fetch\". This\n  required adding an \"is top-level\" flag that gets appropriately plumbed\n  through.\n- Fix #1151 by creating a new algorithm, \"fetch a classic\n  worker-imported script\", which is structured much the same as all other\n  script-fetching algorithms. \"import scripts into worker global scope\"\n  still exists, but it has changed from its previously-separate set of\n  hooks (\"validate the state\", \"get the fetch result\", \"postprocess the\n  fetch result\") to simply using the same \"perform the fetch\" hook.\n- Uniformize the order of parameters passed to the various\n  script-fetching algorithms as much as possible.\n- Correctly extract and use the \"unsafe response\" for all\n  script-fetching that is allowed to bypass CORS.\n- Separate out the \"internal module script tree fetching procedure\"\n  from two now-separate public APIs, \"fetch a module script tree\" and\n  \"fetch a module worker script tree\", which no longer take a number of\n  optional parameters that are not necessary except internally, and no\n  longer require parameters which only make sense specifically in the main\n  page or worker contexts.\n- Clearly delineated the \"public\" script fetching algorithms from the\n  spec-internal ones.\n- Added data-export=\"\" to a variety of algorithms and concepts which the\n  service-worker spec uses.\n",
